From: transentient <cliff.judge@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: retroid: reassemble UART frames and power down MCU + vdd across sleep

Combine Kettle Linux's 1380 + 1441 UART frame reassembly, short-report
filtering, and system sleep PM ops with 1069's home-button pulse
stretch and vdd-supply (vreg_mcu_3v3, TLMM GPIO 3) regulator control.

On Android, Retroid's rs_gpio / mcu_power_control powers down TLMM GPIO 3
(vreg_mcu_3v3), GPIO 109 (reset), and GPIO 111 (enable) whenever the
screen blanks, cutting power to the MCU and all 4 Hall-effect sensors.
With this patch and leds-htr3212 PM ops, vreg_mcu_3v3 reaches 0 use_count
in s2idle and turns off completely.
